.TH FLEXFETCH 1 "August 2026" "flexfetch 0.20.0" 
.SH NAME
flexfetch \- Fast, flexible system info tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBflexfetch\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-modules\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-template\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-gen\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-list\-modules\fR] [\fB\-\-list\-presets\fR] [\fB\-\-list\-themes\fR] [\fB\-\-benchmark\fR] [\fB\-\-pipe\fR] [\fB\-\-minimal\fR] [\fB\-\-flash\fR] [\fB\-\-full\fR] [\fB\-\-dev\fR] [\fB\-\-preset\fR] [\fB\-\-export\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-gradient\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-box\-style\fR] [\fB\-\-palette\-style\fR] [\fB\-\-frame\fR] [\fB\-\-watch\fR] [\fB\-\-watch\-interval\fR] [\fB\-\-live\fR] [\fB\-\-smart\fR] [\fB\-\-health\fR] [\fB\-\-prompt\fR] [\fB\-\-motd\fR] [\fB\-\-ssh\fR] [\fB\-\-diff\fR] [\fB\-\-wizard\fR] [\fB\-\-qr\fR] [\fB\-\-import\-qr\fR] [\fB\-\-update\fR] [\fB\-\-doctor\fR] [\fB\-\-hook\fR] [\fB\-\-update\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-auto\-theme\fR] [\fB\-\-demo\fR] [\fB\-\-bug\-report\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fast, flexible system info tool
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR

.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-modules\fR \fI<MODULES>\fR

.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-template\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: text]

.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI<THEME>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-gen\-config\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-list\-modules\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-list\-presets\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-list\-themes\fR
List all built\-in theme presets (Phase 7.8 — pairs with `\-\-theme random`)
.TP
\fB\-\-benchmark\fR [\fI<BENCHMARK>\fR]
Micro\-benchmark: `\-\-benchmark` (per\-module timing) or `\-\-benchmark N` (run each module N times, report min/avg/total)
.TP
\fB\-\-pipe\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-minimal\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-flash\fR
Fast path (like fastfetch\*(Aqs `flashfetch`): baked\-in defaults, minimal module set, no config file read, no template engine — the fastest possible one\-shot fetch. Only affects the plain terminal render; other modes (\-\-export, \-\-watch, \-\-live, \-\-wizard, \-\-ssh, \-\-diff, \-\-prompt, \-\-motd, \-\-benchmark, \-\-demo) keep their existing behavior
.TP
\fB\-\-full\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-dev\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-preset\fR \fI<PRESET>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-export\fR \fI<EXPORT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-gradient\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-box\-style\fR \fI<BOX_STYLE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-palette\-style\fR \fI<PALETTE_STYLE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-frame\fR \fI<FRAME>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-watch\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-watch\-interval\fR \fI<WATCH_INTERVAL>\fR [default: 2]

.TP
\fB\-\-live\fR
Live dashboard: real\-time CPU/memory gauges, top processes, network rates
.TP
\fB\-\-smart\fR
Smart fetch: add $PWD context (git branch/status, project type, container/venv/SSH)
.TP
\fB\-\-health\fR
Add the system health module (score 0\-100: disk/swap/load/battery)
.TP
\fB\-\-prompt\fR
Single\-line prompt string (e.g. `🐧 arch | CPU 12% | RAM 3.2G`)
.TP
\fB\-\-motd\fR
Plain\-text banner (ANSI colors stripped) for MOTD/startup
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh\fR \fI<SSH>\fR
Fetch remote system info via SSH (repeatable, parallel)
.TP
\fB\-\-diff\fR \fI<DIFF>...\fR
Diff mode (Phase 4.9): compare two systems side\-by\-side. Each target is `local`, `host@remote`, or a path to a flexfetch JSON export file
.TP
\fB\-\-wizard\fR
Interactive config wizard (writes ~/.config/flexfetch/config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-qr\fR
Render the effective config as a terminal QR code (base64+zstd payload, unicode blocks). Scan it with a phone to import on another machine
.TP
\fB\-\-import\-qr\fR \fI<IMPORT_QR>\fR
Import a config from a QR\-code image (PNG/etc; decoded via rqrr) and write it to the config path (existing file is backed up)
.TP
\fB\-\-update\fR
Self\-update: check the latest GitHub release and re\-run the install script if a newer version exists (requires curl)
.TP
\fB\-\-doctor\fR
Environment doctor: validate terminal, color, config, and collectors
.TP
\fB\-\-hook\fR \fI<HOOK>\fR
Print a shell hook (bash|zsh|fish) for cd\-into\-git\-repo context fetches
.TP
\fB\-\-update\-db\fR
Refresh the crowdsourced hardware database (Phase 5.8): downloads the latest PCI/USB name map to the cache dir; falls back to the bundled seed when offline
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-theme\fR
Phase 5.4: derive the theme from the wallpaper\*(Aqs dominant colors (requires the `auto\-theme` feature; falls back to catppuccin otherwise)
.TP
\fB\-\-demo\fR
Phase 8.8: showcase mode — every module + every visual feature, for screenshots / social previews / `install.sh` first\-run demos
.TP
\fB\-\-bug\-report\fR
Phase 8.7: print a full environment/version dump for bug reports (version, OS, kernel, terminal, shell, config, module errors)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
flexfetch\-completions(1)
Generate shell completions for the given shell
.TP
flexfetch\-plugin(1)
Plugin registry (Phase 5.7): search/install/list/update Lua plugins against the hosted registry.toml (checksum + min\-version verified)
.TP
flexfetch\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.20.0
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is loaded from ~/.config/flexfetch/config.toml.
Use \fBflexfetch --gen-config\fR to create a default configuration.

Presets are stored in ~/.config/flexfetch/presets/ as .toml files.

Feature\-gated builds: \fB--no-default-features\fR drops Lua, the live
dashboard, image logos, the Tera template engine, and Rayon for a
~1.5 MB minimal binary (plain \fB||--||\fR tree connectors instead
of templates).
.SH EXAMPLES
Display default modules:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch
.RE

Show only CPU and memory:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch -m cpu:memory
.RE

Export to SVG:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch --export svg -o system.svg
.RE

Use server preset:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch --preset server
.RE

Pipe\-friendly output:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch --pipe | head -20
.RE

Shell prompt string:
.PP
.RS 4
PS1="$(flexfetch --prompt) $ "
.RE

Remote hosts over SSH:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch --ssh server1 --ssh server2
.RE

Configure interactively:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch --wizard
.RE
